{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1375115-advice-of-playing-remotely","id":1375115,"title":"Advice of playing remotely","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-03-16T11:02:00-07:00","id":1375115,"title":"Advice of playing remotely","content":"Hi all.<br /> <br /> Due to the Covid 19 pandemic, its likely that where I live will soon be under lock down sufficient to stop face to face RP sessions. I'm about to run an exalted game that I've been writing for ages and rather than no roleplaying, I'm going to try and do it using all the wonderful tools we now have to connect us.<br /> <br /> I've played in games before over google hangouts and discord, and I've recently become aware of virtual gaming environments/supports like Roll20, Fantasy Grounds and D20Pro. These products seem mostly to cater for the DnD/pathfinder type market. Does anyone know of any products that either support Exalted explicitly or that you have used for exalted and have had a positive experience with. <br /> <br /> Has anyone run exalted online? What was easy about it and what were the drawbacks? Has anyone got any good tools they can share specific to online play?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4249-gribblethemunchkin","name":"gribblethemunchkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4249_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-16T11:23:28-07:00","id":1375122,"title":"","content":"We have used Google Hangouts pretty successfully (Mostly for Savage Worlds gaming)... But, as with all things, YMMV.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":540,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","user":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","date":". 03-16-2020, 02:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-16T11:34:24-07:00","id":1375125,"title":"","content":"My group uses Roll20 just for rolling (and keeping the character sheets when possible), and we play Scion 2e (there are character sheets) and Aberrant 2e (we use Scion character sheat).<br /> <br /> We played 2d20 and Aberrant for a while without in app sheaths, using Google docs to share every thing. We used Roll20 for only rolling the dice and draw maps when needed.<br /> <br /> I may be wrong, but I think there is at least the Exalted char sheaths in Roll20, and the dice rolling is quite easy too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-16T12:08:55-07:00","id":1375133,"title":"","content":"I found Discord got confusing, actually, without the video function.<br /> <br /> We've used skype for ages, but... yeah, Skype isn't that good. I might see if my friends want to try Google Meet or Hangouts instead. Not a huge difference, just a bit better, but you can share stuff if you want to, say, have a map or picture come up instead of your face. I used it today to teach a class.<br /> <br /> Zoom I think would be best, or some other software that has breakout rooms, so that if the PCs are seperated, they can have in-character conversations while the DM is doing something else. I sometimes type IC conversations on steam with some other players while the ST is doing something with another character.<br /> A lot of those you have to pay for though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 03-16-2020, 05:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-16T13:43:47-07:00","id":1375140,"title":"","content":"I use IRC because we can't be bothered to update to Discord.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-16T15:02:10-07:00","id":1375154,"title":"","content":"I would suggest a play-by-post. Have the characters describe how they want to fight in combats in advance (&quot;I want to use a 2m Excellency and 3m Force of the Mountain Smash attacks on every round, spending from Peripheral so my anima flares and Decisiving if my enemy is in Crash&quot;) and have the ST roll it all out on their side. And follow the advice in the Corebook of having 2-5 combat charms including at least one Ox-Body.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-17T00:37:07-07:00","id":1375233,"title":"","content":"I find play-by-post to be sloooow.<br /> Although you get better stunts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-17T00:49:00-07:00","id":1375235,"title":"","content":"Oh, I also find play-by-post to be more serious. Whether that's a good thing, you decide.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-18T09:51:03-07:00","id":1375447,"title":"","content":"For about two years now, I've been running a chronicle via Roll20 -- we use it for rolls, character sheets, handouts, etc. I have pages with stuff like the map of Creation, a Creation calendar, etc. (I even calibrated the measuring tool on the map page to give an accurate-to-scale reading in miles, because why not.)<br /> <br /> The Roll20 character sheet for Exalted is pretty good; there's a space under the Charm entries where you can put notes or even copy-paste the full Charm text. I do wish there was more support in the form of macros, a way to handle double 10's automatically and what-not.<br /> <br /> We did end up moving to Discord for our voice chat, though, because the Roll20 integrated voice thing proved to be pretty unreliable for us.<br /> <br /> Let me share our (bare-bones) macros:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Roll:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_description\">Code:</div> <pre class=\"bbcode_code notranslate\" style=\"max-height:calc(30 * 1.4rem + 2 * var(--bbcode-padding) + var(--h-scrollbar-allowance));\">/me rolls to ?{I roll to...|forget to signpost} /roll ?{Pool|0}d10&gt;7sd</pre> </div>Secret-Roll (to send a roll straight to the GM without posting it in the general chat):<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_description\">Code:</div> <pre class=\"bbcode_code notranslate\" style=\"max-height:calc(30 * 1.4rem + 2 * var(--bbcode-padding) + var(--h-scrollbar-allowance));\">/w gm I roll to ?{I roll to...|forget to signpost} /gmroll ?{Pool|0}d10&gt;7sd</pre> </div>Join-Battle (you have to select the token of whoever's rolling JB to add them to the tracker properly):<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_description\">Code:</div> <pre class=\"bbcode_code notranslate\" style=\"max-height:calc(30 * 1.4rem + 2 * var(--bbcode-padding) + var(--h-scrollbar-allowance));\">/roll ?{Pool|0}d10&gt;7sd +3 &amp;{tracker}</pre> </div>Attack:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_description\">Code:</div> <pre class=\"bbcode_code notranslate\" style=\"max-height:calc(30 * 1.4rem + 2 * var(--bbcode-padding) + var(--h-scrollbar-allowance));\">/me attacks ?{I attack...|the foe} /roll ?{Attack Pool|0}d10&gt;7sd-?{Defense|0}</pre> </div>Damage:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_description\">Code:</div> <pre class=\"bbcode_code notranslate\" style=\"max-height:calc(30 * 1.4rem + 2 * var(--bbcode-padding) + var(--h-scrollbar-allowance));\">/roll (?{Threshold|0} + ?{Damage|0} - ?{Soak|0})d10&gt;7sd</pre> </div></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7058-kerredai","name":"Kerredai","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-18T09:51:43-07:00","id":1375448,"title":"","content":"I find Blue-Booking (or Journaling) to be an awesome addition to any game environment, but particularly for Remote play. Adds a lot of depth in my opinion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-18T10:56:58-07:00","id":1375456,"title":"","content":"My preferred medium is Discord for both PBP and voice. There's a dicebot called D10 you can find if you search &quot;exalted discord dicebot&quot;, and it's got lots of dicetricks baked in (doubling numbers, rerolling numbers, automatic successes, nondoubling tens, target number shifting, etc). Making a little server for your game allows for things like a different channel for the ST to talk with each player about their character in, and multiple IC channels for text stuff if that fits your needs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans","name":"Beans","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8026_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"472"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-21T10:14:13-07:00","id":1375978,"title":"","content":"I have to ask: are you recruiting more people to your game? Id love to join one now that I, too, am locked into my house for the foreseeable future.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2548-worrowindxvi","name":"WorrowindXVI","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-22T16:15:19-07:00","id":1376168,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the ideas guys, am gonna try Roll20 and see what it can do.<br /> <br /> WorrowindXVI - Sorry dude, I already have potentially 5 players which is already the most I like to run for face to face, let alone online.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4249-gribblethemunchkin","name":"gribblethemunchkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4249_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-23T13:20:03-07:00","id":1376298,"title":"","content":"Roll20 has everything I need to run a game (except the whiskey). I highly recommend it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kerredai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1375115-advice-of-playing-remotely?p=1375447#post1375447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... a way to handle double 10's automatically...</div> </div> </div> </div>I handle double 10s, and successes more generally, with their custom tables feature.<br /> <br /> A table with these frequencies covers most of the rolls, which I call TN7 for target number 7:<br /> <br /> Botch: 1 (these are 1's on a d10, but writing 'Botch' I found works best)<br /> 0: 5 (these are the 2's through 6's on a a d10)<br /> 1: 3 (7, 8, 9)<br /> 2: 1 (10)<br /> <br /> Bonus, the roll on the table adds up the successes. <br /> <br /> But I find for more advanced xp chronicles, you'll need TN6, Dub9's, Dub8's, No5s, etc. etc. which is just some fiddling with the frequencies of the success counts.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}